KG42.register("clusters-7f4b2c469ffaed58b0e72111",{"id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v142-d-CL003","paper":"23-hierarchical_market_structure","label":"LA price-spread roles and role 2 cross-market offer interface","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"LA price-spread roles and role 2 cross-market offer interface","market_meaning":"LA forms two cross-market trading roles based on the comparison between the DNEM MCP and its WEM bus LMP; role 2 further uses the DNEM price and a constrained strategy to form WEM offers. The general import/export quantity and local clearing quantity establish an interface that retains local roles, but the existing chain cannot yet guarantee actual transactions or a complete cross-market equilibrium.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM_DEM","DEM"],"process_stages":["activation","coordination","pricing","clearing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The two price-spread conditions of R009 are retained separately, and R008 applies only to role 2. R004 provides the DNEM price source, while R002 shares only the general import/export quantity interface; its Case 1 result does not become a premise of this cluster. The historical quantity branch of the single-LA algorithm and the price-spread comparison are not regarded as equivalent conditions, and prices and quantities across iterations are not assumed to be synchronized by default.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The choice of trading direction and the role 2 offer share a source-defined DNEM price and are undertaken by the same LA for cross-market activity, giving them functional complementarity; they are distinct from DNO local clearing and case-specific revenue. The conditions for strictly positive transaction quantity, the WEM receiving side, and the timing sequence are not yet closed.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Retain the role semantics of the two price-spread conditions and of equal-quantity cross-market purchase and sale, while disclosing the limitations of the existing logical translation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplement the activity in which role 2 uses the DNEM price to form WEM offers and strategy bounds."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Cite only the DNEM MCP identity and the responsibility for providing it, and do not count local price formation again as a new rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Cite the local role of the general import/export quantity in DNEM clearing, and do not treat the Case 1 result or the historical quantity branch as proof of the price-spread conditions."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_0","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The MCP corresponding to the DNEM balancing multiplier is explicitly used as a price input by the role 2 offer expression; this interface identifies the price source and does not itself determine which iteration's value the algorithm adopts."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The DNEM comparison price for the two roles and the MCP provided by the DNO have the same source definition; the WEM bus LMP remains another price and is not merged with it."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E011"],"rationale":"The source separately explains, for role 2, the price-spread direction, the purchase/sale role, and the construction of the WEM offer, so they can be assembled complementarily; the offer expression is not generalized to role 1, and no execution edge is added from narrative order."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x-P_l_imp"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E000","v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"Under the same LA and aligned market states, the DNEM allocated import quantity corresponds to the cross-market transaction quantity of role 1; this interface does not guarantee that any positive price spread obtains strictly positive dispatch."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN011","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-P_l_exp"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E000","v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g02-E12"],"rationale":"Role 2's DNEM export quantity is used as a preset balancing input in local clearing; this is a different model role of the same import/export definition, and this input must not be mistakenly written as a new DNO decision quantity."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_0","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"Both are identified by the source as the MCP of the same DNEM and are used respectively for the role 2 offer and the price-spread comparison; their uses and value time points remain independent, and the price values of different iterations are not claimed to be equal."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x-P_l_imp","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E000","v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The terminology definition and the description of the two market roles support the identity of the same LA's DNEM import power; the clearing use and the trading role are retained separately, and actual numerical correspondence still requires aligned market states."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-P_l_exp","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E000","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"Both refer to the power exported by the LA from the DNEM; their role as an input parameter in the clearing chain and their role as an operating quantity in the trading chain cannot be collapsed into a single rewritten object."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM008","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"Both places explicitly refer to the DNEM MCP and have the same scope of application, so R004 may be selected as the display representative; this mapping does not include the R009 node that also carries the WEM price comparison."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R009's equivalent translation directs the price spread directly to strictly positive transaction quantity, but it does not simultaneously express allocation and capacity feasibility, equal-quantity purchase and sale in the two markets, or the treatment when prices are equal. After linking with R002's quantity limitation, it cannot be used to guarantee that a positive price spread necessarily produces positive traded volume.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream review should verify the logical direction and the strictly positive quantity interpretation, and clarify transaction feasibility, the equal-quantity relationship, and boundary cases; keep the current expression frozen and do not fabricate conditions in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G002","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R002 selects the parameter branch according to the import/export quantity at the reference time point, R009 describes roles according to the price comparison, and the R008 price input is also affected by observability and the algorithm's price carry-over; these roles and time points cannot be directly equated.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_0","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E025","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should clarify the iteration correspondence between the role judgment and the quantity and price snapshots; the same-quantity mapping retains only the identity of quantity and does not replace proof of time-point consistency."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R008's role 2 revenue objective and the WEM clearing, capacity, and LMP formation processes do not form a supplied chain. The existing LMP parameter in R009 cannot make up for the WEM price attribution and the complete role 2 model pointed out by R008's current C2 revision request.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E017"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g03-wholesale-lmp"],"required_work":"Upstream should supplement the necessary role 2 revenue and WEM receiving-side rules according to the source, and handle the existing C2 revision request; this cluster retains only the offer and role interface candidates."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G004","category":"ontology_extension","description":"R009 binds the WEM bus LMP to pricing.local, which may mix wholesale node prices with the DNEM MCP; at the same time, the existing framework does not explicitly express the LA's dual-market intermediary identity as a strategic trader. The LA must not be equated with the DNO merely because it undertakes interface activities.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta001","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E018"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g03-wholesale-lmp","v141-b-g01-P01","v141-b-g02-P01","proposal:v141-b-g03-load-aggregator"],"required_work":"Manually check the WEM price, the LA intermediary proposal, and the existing binding; the proposal remains unapproved, and no new node is created or intermediary role merged into the local operator."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G005","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The unit of the R008 offer vector is $/MW, the MCP input is in $/MWh, and the strategy quantity is given no unit; the time or unit convention of the existing product expression is not closed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_rho_prime_l","v141-c-R008::x::x_psi_prime_l","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_0","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E000","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g02-E20"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the source's offer, strategy, and pricing time units, and have upstream clarify the conversion convention; the strategy must not be assumed dimensionless or the time period assumed to be 1 hour."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G006","category":"unverified_source","description":"The role, price interface, and quantity identity mappings are based solely on experimentally permitted unverified evidence; this cluster does not mean that the B transcription, the existing C logical translation, or the scientific conclusions have undergone independent review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E000","v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually verify the price-spread conditions, units, and iteration meanings, and then evaluate the candidate interfaces and mathematical completeness."}]},"rule_refs":["23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R009","23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R008","23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R004","23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R002"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-44ec202cc152796d","KG31-42e78591f3f99231","KG31-589dd70d32471060","KG31-e9831a630acebd8d","KG40-45833afd23977831"]});
